## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end reasoning across CNPA components, focusing on correctness under concurrent event processing and deployment scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end tracing
- Kafka producer ordering
- Consumer offset management
- Redis cache invalidation
- Event versioning and idempotent sinks
- Cache stampede protection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example snippet: idempotent sink for Redis
async function sinkEvent(event) {
  const key = event.key;
  const ver = event.version;
  const current = await redis.get(key);
  if (!current || current.version < ver) {
    await redis.set(key, JSON.stringify(event));
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
End-to-end tracing across HTTP, DB, Kafka, and Redis helps diagnose issues that span services and reveals propagation gaps.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry
- Trace Context propagation
- Span lifetimes and sampling
- Exporters and collectors

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry setup and propagation
const tracer = opentelemetry.trace.getTracer('cnpa');
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('HTTP '+ req.path);
  req.span = span;
  res.on('finish', ()=> span.end());
  next();
});
```

